{"text": "Here are a few possibilities:  1.", "source": "lang_non_fr", "sha1": "e32f59122b315c7821931331d31c450bb57d59ae"}
{"text": "**Passer**: This is a verb that means \"to pass\" or \"to go by\".", "source": "lang_non_fr", "sha1": "cc68e81e3273ae3c1cf93e503bab86bc2e798606"}
{"text": "It can refer", "source": "lang_non_fr", "sha1": "ab1cd9414aced55845bb4ace06c545a5123a17ea"}
{"text": "to", "source": "lang_non_fr", "sha1": "d20f96e862ac9b6740b01301fb9783c3578dd337"}
{"text": ":    - A vehicle passing by    - A person", "source": "lang_non_fr", "sha1": "910b03c348b3684d0a61c918346cb5a2c1ddbf19"}
{"text": "passing", "source": "lang_non_fr", "sha1": "292ae8c49ec690193e9062fc9a460a9d6e824185"}
{"text": "through a place", "source": "lang_non_fr", "sha1": "108186e2ae026bd9e0d7fe6003ba7c62946f9ded"}
